Add type checking to generics.

### Use case

I want to determine the type of a generic, but methods like T==List cannot meet my needs.
Because T may be either a List<String>or a List<int>, the method of T==List cannot be used to determine the type of T.
I used another method to determine the type of T, but I hope to have a simple way like T==List to determine the type of T.
Here is my partial code

AcadsocResponse.fromJson(dynamic json, {T Function(dynamic)? fromJson}) {
// final defaultBody = T == List ? (json['Body'] ?? []) : (json['Body'] ?? {});
final defaultBody =
checkTIsList() ? (json['Body'] ?? []) : (json['Body'] ?? {});
body = fromJson != null ? fromJson(defaultBody) : defaultBody;
errorCode = json['ErrorCode'] ?? -1;
msg = json['Msg'] ?? '';
isSuccess = json['IsSuccess'] ?? false;
}
bool checkTIsList() {
final arr = T.toString().split("<");
if (arr.firstOrNull == 'List') {
return true;
}
return false;
}

